::warning file=domain/entities.go,line=7,col=1,title=W003 PostgreSQL column exists but is unmapped::column public.events.note is not mapped%0A%0Athe column is nullable, so inserts succeed without it, but its value cannot be read back%0A%0AFix: add a field for note to domain.Event, or leave it unmapped on purpose and set strict.unmapped_columns: off
::warning file=domain/entities.go,line=12,col=2,title=W015 timestamp without time zone::public.events.happened is timestamp without time zone%0A%0Athe column stores a wall clock reading with no offset, so the instant it denotes depends on whoever reads it%0A%0AFix: change the column to timestamptz, or set strict.timestamp_without_tz: off if the ambiguity is intended
